                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please update the names as per nomenclature mentioned in downstream doc (CC @Kevin.Tung@quantatw.com )"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb.json",
                    "line": 732,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Change to Harma_MB_CPLD"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please add the compatible hardware to phosphor-dbus-interfaces."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please update this as per https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/80551/2/yaml/com/meta/Hardware/Harma.interface.yaml."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please confirm if the same FW image will be used for both the Harma mb versions or its different?\nIn case its different we cannot use the same CompatibleHardware tag."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Change to \"com.meta.Hardware.Harma.CPLD.LCMXO3LF_4300C\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "@paligill@gmail.com, it's true that we've never had a design where a single board includes two CPLDs. However, in past projects, we did implement measures to prevent flashing the wrong image across different boards. So changing it to something like 'com.meta.Hardware.CPLD.MB.LCMXO3LF_4300C' might be a good choice."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> @paligill@gmail.com, it's true that we've never had a design where a single board includes two CPLDs. However, in past projects, we did implement measures to prevent flashing the wrong image across different boards. So changing it to something like 'com.meta.Hardware.CPLD.MB.LCMXO3LF_4300C' might be a good choice.\n\n@Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com I suppose its better if we have a dedicated CompatibleHardware tag in case there is a variation between CLD FW images. Also, it will cut short the validation at the software level as package validation will itself fail. Having said that does the 2 instances you covered in this patch use the same image or different? In case its different then we should have more info embedded in PDI definition for this to specify so."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 416,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "The two instances share the same image because they are the main source and the second source, respectively, but both are MB CPLDs.\nHowever, the CPLDs in the system still might not share the same image even if they use the same chip; add a suffix to distinguish them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 419,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please update the names as per nomenclature mentioned in downstream doc."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 419,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Change to Harma_MB_CPLD"
                }
            ],
